This mathematical page fixes the $(-,+,+,+)$ metric, the SI-to-natural potential and charge normalizations, the covariant derivative $D_a=\partial_a-ig a_a$, and the finite-mode commuting-spinor convention. It constructs the positive transverse photon space, the subsidiary null quotient, the Lorentz-covariant massless representation, smeared potentials, and local gauge-invariant field-strength and Weyl observables. The periodic Gauss solver is stated only for smooth neutral data on a flat torus; the charged Dirac variation is conditional on the inspected free-action interface. The transverse potential is nonlocal, while the field strength is local. Auxiliary timelike vectors are not physical quotient states, and no global continuous real polarization frame exists. These are mathematical free/classical deductions, not an adoption of a measured $\mu_0$, a charge-quantization rule, an interacting continuum QED construction, or an experimental result. The QFT-MF02/MF03/MF04 draft interfaces are used only at their inspected statements and remain subject to their recorded readiness status.
